Where an upstream LLVM build of this kernel (macOS-DroidVM builds it with LLVM 21 on Linux) lacks what Apple clang has, each
under a test of the compiler, so the Apple clang builds of this repository are unchanged:
- kalloc types: no __builtin_xnu_type_summary/_types_compatible/_type_signature. Every type counts as data (KT_SUMMARY_GRANULES),
  pointer compatibility checks pass, signatures are empty; kalloc_type_view_init_fixed/_var return at a count of 0 instead
  of asserting (nothing to place); and the views of Apple's kexts, which carry their real type signatures, are made data
  only too, so kernel and kexts follow one heap policy.
- libkern/os/base.h: no "authenticates-null-values" __ptrauth option; null stays unsigned (only xnu-private fields use
  OS_PTRAUTH_SIGNED_PTR_AUTH_NULL).
From macOS-DroidVM patches/xnu-12377/0002 (kalloc.h, IOLib.h), 0006 (the empty-view guard) and 0007 (kext views, base.h)
(lateautumn233).

diff --git a/iokit/IOKit/IOLib.h b/iokit/IOKit/IOLib.h
index 6b9d740..ebfa41b 100644
--- a/iokit/IOKit/IOLib.h
+++ b/iokit/IOKit/IOLib.h
@@ -96,10 +96,15 @@ IOMallocArraySize(vm_size_t hdr_size, vm_size_t elem_size, vm_size_t elem_count)
 	return s;
 }
 
+#if __has_builtin(__builtin_xnu_types_compatible)
 #define IOKIT_TYPE_IS_COMPATIBLE_PTR(ptr, type) \
 	(__builtin_xnu_types_compatible(os_get_pointee_type(ptr), type) ||   \
 	    __builtin_xnu_types_compatible(os_get_pointee_type(ptr), void))  \
 
+#else
+#define IOKIT_TYPE_IS_COMPATIBLE_PTR(ptr, type) 1 /* upstream LLVM: no type compatibility builtin */
+#endif
+
 #define IOKIT_TYPE_ASSERT_COMPATIBLE_POINTER(ptr, type) \
 	_Static_assert(IOKIT_TYPE_IS_COMPATIBLE_PTR(ptr, type), \
 	    "Pointer type is not compatible with specified type")
